; Inside an arithmetic expression, four or more digits then twice a dash or a
; slash and digits are a date, as at the start of any word, so each
; transaction is dropped; three digits before the dash are a subtraction,
; and two dashes in a row a subtraction of a negative number.
2020-01-01 open Assets:A
2020-01-01 open Assets:B

2020-01-02 *
  Assets:A  (2020-1-2) USD
  Assets:B

2020-01-03 *
  Assets:A  (1 + 2020/01/02) USD
  Assets:B

2020-01-04 *
  Assets:A  -(2020-01-02) USD
  Assets:B

2020-01-05 *
  Assets:A  (3 - 12020-1-2) USD
  Assets:B

2020-01-06 *
  Assets:A  (999-1-2) USD
  Assets:A  (2020--5) USD
  Assets:A  (1000.5*2) USD
  Assets:B

2020-01-07 balance Assets:A  5022.0 USD
